# Pump the chamber to high vacuum with the turbo
# Closes the vent, fill and gate valves, turns the turbo pump off and waits for it
# to stop turning (at once if it was off), closes the foreline valve, starts the
# vacuum pump and waits 15 s, then
# roughs the chamber to the 0.01 Torr crossover, for at most an hour. Closes the vacuum
# valve, opens the foreline valve, starts the turbo pump and gives it 5 minutes to spin
# up (its speed is not read). Checks the chamber is still at the crossover, opens the
# gate valve and waits, for at most the hours given, for the pressure. The turbo pump,
# the foreline and gate valves and the vacuum pump stay as they are until seal chamber
# or the end of the run. This path has not yet been run on this chamber: watch the
# first run at the HMI.
block highvac to <pressure:number 0.0000001..0.01 Torr> within <hours:number 1..48 h>
load rLACO

hvc vent close
hvc fill close
hvc gate close
hvc turbo off
until TurboSpinning = false
hvc foreline close
hvc pump on
hold 15 s
until chamberP >= 0.01 within 30 s
hvc rough open
until chamberP <= 0.01 within 60 min
hvc rough close
hvc foreline open
hvc turbo on
hold 5 min
until chamberP <= 0.01 within 1 min
hvc gate open
until chamberP < {pressure} within {hours} h
